content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive with the breakpoint name, inside your own CSS:

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;
  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

- The docs show `@variant` only with `dark` and `hover` (`src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx`, `@variant` section; `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Using variants"). The same syntax should work for responsive variants like `md`, but the docs don't show that example.
- Breakpoint names and their media queries, such as `md` = `@media (width >= 48rem)`, are in `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Targeting a breakpoint range" and "Customizing your theme".
- You can also write the media query yourself, using `theme(--breakpoint-md)` in `@media (width >= theme(--breakpoint-md))`. This form appears in `src/docs/upgrade-guide.mdx`, "Using the theme() function".

